 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Home console: 150 old models turned into 41 platform-family archetypes ordered by generation (revisions and regional names as versions, all from fetched Wikipedia pages); 40 lesser platforms kept as flat models. FPGA, clone and licensed re-release machines (Analogue, MiSTer, Hyperkin RetroN, Retro-Bit, Polymega, Atari 2600+/7800+, AtGames, M64) moved to the new FPGA & clone console kind. Old data credited the M64 to Plaion; the fetched source shows the maker is ModRetro, so corrected. Moved to other shelves: THE400 Mini, THEA500 Mini, THEC64 Mini, X68000 Z, Sport Vii, Xavix PORT (to Plug-and-play & mini console, 00_02); PlayStation TV (Vita-family micro-console, to Handhelds & hybrids 00_01). Magnavox Odyssey (1972) left to the dedicated-console shelf as planned there. Dropped to stay within 40 flat models: DVD Kids (3-Plus), Champion 2711 (Unisonic), CT510 (eedoo) (least-documented). Videopac+ G7400, AV Famicom, Wii mini, Neo Geo CD, Panasonic Q, iQue Player, Beena etc. are now versions. Wikidata was rate-limited (HTTP 429); all sources are fetched Wikipedia pages plus one CNX Software article. | Coordinator: maker renamed \"Bally Manufacturing\" so the register does not merge it with the Swiss fashion house Bally."
